* PieceSpice Tier-4 ideal-switch model for cpm2-1200
* Method: standard SPICE ideal voltage-controlled switch + offline LUT
* Losses handled offline in thermal post-processing (cf. PLECS P-TC).
* Standard SPICE SW primitive; no PLECS/SIMPLIS step-count or speed
* behavior is claimed for this emitted model.
* waveform_gate: retired_by_design
* Retired observables: dv/dt [INFERENCE], Miller droop (P-DEMO Fig. 6),
*   ringing [INFERENCE], reverse recovery (P-DEMO Fig. 7), voltage-
*   dependent capacitances, body-diode switching waveform.  dv/dt and
*   ringing are inferred from instantaneous switching and absent
*   parasitics; P-DEMO names the transient, Miller droop and recovery.
* These do not exist in this ideal-switch tier's electrical solution;
* energy/efficiency vs golden is scored offline, not on a converter bench.
* One measured LINEAR C_QOSS (Curve-4 Coss at cap_ref_Vds) is active only
* as a solver stabilizer: it slows drain dv/dt and adds L-C overshoot, so
* the DPT waveform gate stays retired_by_design.  It only prevents
* singular / no-capacitance solver steps; it is NOT a voltage-dependent
* or waveform-fidelity capacitance model.  Voltage-dependent capacitors
* and the body diode remain retired (see above).

.SUBCKT cpm2-1200_PIECESPICE_T4 d g s
* Pins: d=drain g=gate s=source (positional; gate threshold Vgs=V(g,s))

* --- ideal conduction (Curve-3 rds_on, measured Roff, switch Vt) ---
* temperature_c = 25 (reference temperature; config conditions.temperature)
* data_limitation: E_on/E_off and r_on are measured only at this
*   conditions.temperature = 25 C; the LUT has no temperature
*   axis and is valid only there.  It is a measured data slice, not a
*   physical guarantee at other junction temperatures.
*   The current 2x2 grid has 4 finite measured node(s) (capability 'grid_interpolation'); 1 complete 2x2 cell(s) allow bilinear interpolation; other off-node queries are NaN.
*   Losses are evaluated offline.
*   They are not electrical power consumed by this switch (P-TC:
*   Conduction Losses / Switching Losses notes).
* vth_v = 2.46720941 (Curve-7 JEDEC threshold, config/outputs/<vendor>/curve7_threshold_voltage.yaml)
* vt_switch_v = 2.46720941 (source=curve7_jedec_vth; no finite config/LUT switching threshold; the emitted switch uses the measured Curve-7 JEDEC threshold)
* r_on_ohms = 0.0281695701 (Curve-3 rds_on at 20 V, conditions.Vgs_fixed; selection: nearest measured current point to i_load_a=20 A (runtime selection))
* r_on_source = r_on_ohms (vgs_on_v=18; vgs_points=[])
* vgs_on_v = 18 (config dpt.vgs_on; gate-drive metadata only)
* r_off_ohms = 4270438.96 (source=measured_vgs0_dc_sweep; measured at Vgs=0 DC sweep as Roff=Vbus/Ioff; full provenance in source.r_off)
* vh_v = 0 (source=project_decision: zero hysteresis, switch tracks the selected threshold)
S_SW d s g s SW_T4
.MODEL SW_T4 SW(Ron=0.0281695701 Roff=4270438.96 Vt=2.46720941 Vh=0)
* --- one measured linear output capacitor: solver stabilizer only ---
* coss_f = 1.85775652e-09 F (source=measured_curve4_capacitance; Curve-4 Coss at cap_ref_Vds; provenance in source.coss)
C_QOSS d s 1.85775652e-09

* --- loss lookup data: COMMENT / METADATA ONLY (no active elements) ---
* Energy is computed offline by pipeline.tier4 at the measured switching
* current and applied thermally; no E/G source consumes these tables.
* vbus_points = [20, 800]
* current_points = [10, 20]
* temperature_points = [25]
* e_on_uj[vbus][current], microjoules (NaN = no golden crossing):
